    "done_when": "The classifier in reckon/crew/recovery.py never reports a live run as \"unwritten\" in two transient states. (a) Within the launch-window grace after dispatch, before the worker has written its orientation manifest: the run reads as it did before, dispatched or working. (b) While its manifest is being rewritten in place: a manifest file that is smaller than the last one read, or modified within the last few seconds, and does not parse is treated as unchanged, and the previous classification stands. Workers write manifests by hand, so this is a reader-side fix only. Measured on 2026-09-26: unmanaged-producer-keeps-a-log went working → unwritten → working within 12 s, 40 s after launch, before its orientation manifest existed. plan-reads-stay-in-the-worktree went working → unwritten → working in 9 s while its manifest was 4 bytes mid-rewrite. tests/test_a_run_in_motion_is_not_unwritten.py uses tmp_path (the pytest fixture), with every crew directory environment-resolved to tmp_path and a live stub pid. Case 1: a live run dispatched 30 s ago with no manifest yet is not classified unwritten. Case 2: a live run whose previous read was working, now with a 4-byte manifest modified 1 s ago, is not classified unwritten. Case 3: a live run past the grace with no manifest still reads unwritten, so the guard keeps its purpose. Negative control: remove the grace and the mid-rewrite tolerance; cases 1 and 2 must fail. tests/test_crew_recovery.py adds no failures against the base, with pytest basetemp outside any git repository. Gate and control logs are written under the run directory. The change is committed in this worktree.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Keep the classifier from reporting unwritten for a run inside its launch window or mid-rewrite of its manifest.",
